# SWHP Frontend Implementation Plan

This document outlines the detailed plan to develop the frontend for the Single Window Health Portal (SWHP) using a **feature-based architecture** powered by **Next.js**.

## 1. Frontend Architecture & Setup
- **Framework:** Next.js (App Router for native file-system routing).
- **Styling & UI Library:** Ant Design (antd) for a comprehensive, enterprise-grade component suite. `@ant-design/nextjs-registry` handles SSR styling.
- **State Management:** React Context API and local state hooks (no Redux).
- **HTTP Client:** Axios for API communication, configured with interceptors.
- **Directory Structure:** Feature-based slicing within the `src/` directory.

### Directory Structure (Feature-Based)
```text
src/
+-- app/             # Next.js App Router (Pages & Layouts)
¦   +-- login/page.jsx
¦   +-- register/page.jsx
¦   +-- apply/page.jsx
¦   +-- dashboard/page.jsx
¦   +-- layout.jsx
¦   +-- page.jsx
+-- components/      # Shared global components (Navbar, Footer)
+-- lib/             # Shared utilities, Axios instance setup
+-- features/        # Feature modules
¦   +-- auth/        # Login, Register, AccountMapping, AuthContext
¦   +-- profile/     # UserProfile form and state
¦   +-- services/    # Service Selection checklist and SWAN initialization
¦   +-- application/ # iFrame orchestrator, postMessage listener, progress tracker
¦   +-- payment/     # Fee aggregation UI, Gateway redirect logic
¦   +-- tracking/    # Unified tracking dashboard table
```

### Phase 1: Project Initialization & Routing
- [ ] Scaffold Next.js application (`npx create-next-app@latest`).
- [ ] Install dependencies: `axios`, `antd`, `@ant-design/icons`, `@ant-design/nextjs-registry`.
- [ ] Setup folder structure aligning with feature-based architecture (`src/features/...`).
- [ ] Implement `RootLayout` in `src/app/layout.jsx` integrating Ant Design Registry and AuthContext.

## 2. Core Features Implementation

### Phase 2: `features/auth` & `features/profile`
- [ ] **Auth Components:** Create `Login`, `Register`, and `AccountMapping` components under `src/features/auth/components`. Use Ant Design's `<Form>`.
- [ ] **Auth Context:** Implement `AuthContext.jsx` in `src/features/auth/context` for JWT management.
- [ ] **Profile Management:** Create the `UserProfile` form under `src/features/profile/components`.

### Phase 3: `features/services` (Selection & SWAN)
- [ ] **Service Checklist:** Build `ServiceList.jsx` displaying available legacy services using antd `<Card>`.
- [ ] **SWAN Flow:** Create `hooks/useSwan.js` inside `features/services` to call `/api/v1/swan/create`.

### Phase 4: `features/application` (iFrame Orchestration)
- [ ] **iFrame Container:** Create `ServiceIframe.jsx` in `features/application/components`.
- [ ] **postMessage Listener:** Implement `hooks/usePostMessage.js` inside the application feature. Validate origins and payloads.
- [ ] **Queue Management:** Build `ApplicationOrchestrator.jsx` to advance through selected services using antd `<Steps>`.

### Phase 5: `features/payment` & `features/tracking`
- [ ] **Payment UI:** Build `FeeSummary.jsx` in `features/payment/components` to fetch from `/api/v1/swan/{swan}/fees`.
- [ ] **Tracking Dashboard:** Build `TrackingTable.jsx` in `features/tracking/components` using antd `<Table>`.

## 3. Security & Validation
- [ ] Apply **CAPTCHA** to auth forms.
- [ ] Implement **Strict Origin Validation** on all incoming `postMessage` events.
- [ ] Ensure **CSRF Protection** (handled via stateless JWT).
